hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3072","**\nNarrated to us 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir, narrated to us Ibn Numayr, on the authority of 'Ubaydullah, on the authority of Sumayy, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurayrah (RA) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:\n\n\An 'Umrah to another 'Umrah expiates for what is between them"," and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise.\"""""
"3073","Narrated to us Abd al-Jabbar ibn al-Ala', who narrated to us Sufyan, who said: It was narrated to me by Sumay. And narrated to us Hawtharah ibn Muhammad, who narrated to us Sufyan, on the authority of Sumay, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah (RA), who reported that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Umrah performed after another Umrah expiates all sins committed between the two"," and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise.\"" However"," Abd al-Jabbar stated that the narration is traced through him [Sumay"," i.e."," his chain of narration terminates at Sumay without the intermediate narrators present in the second full chain]."""
